        "title": "US eases restrictions on Apple’s access to AI chips and data center equipment in the UAE",
        "url": "https://9to5mac.com/2026/07/10/us-eases-restrictions-on-apples-access-to-ai-chips-and-data-center-equipment-in-the-uae/",
        "content_text": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/04/Analysts-believe-Apple-taking-a-highly-unusual-step-to-double-Mac-user-base.jpg?quality=82&#038;strip=all&#038;w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Apple is among eight U.S. companies now able to bring covered advanced-computing chips, servers, and other controlled technology into the UAE without applying for individual export licenses. Here’s what that means.</p>",
