        "content_text": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/07/Siri-AI-can-pull-info-from-third-party-apps-in-the-latest-developer-beta.jpg?quality=82&#038;strip=all&#038;w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">We’ve been looking out for <a href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/07/06/heres-whats-new-with-ios-27-beta-3/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">new features</a> in <a href=\"https://9to5mac.com/guides/ios-27/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">iOS 27</a> beta 3, and we’ve now found an additional one: the latest developer beta allows <a href=\"https://9to5mac.com/guides/siri/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Siri AI</a> to access information from third-party apps.</p>\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The only examples seen so far are pulling in the remaining battery from electric car apps, but it’s likely that other capabilities will be found …</p>",
